   "flags": {},
   "order": 1,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "HEAD SWAP (BFS LoRA)\n\n1. Picture 1: the body. Its body, pose, outfit, hands, location and lighting stay.\n2. Picture 2: the head. Its face, facial expression, hairstyle and hair color are moved onto the body.\n3. Press Run.\n\nKeep the words 'head_swap:' at the start of the prompt; the BFS LoRA was trained on that wording. Uses the 'alternative' BFS LoRA: in tests the regular v1.1 one left a crosshatch texture over the whole picture. Keep both LoRAs at 1.0; lower strengths gave a broken, noisy image.\n\nTips\n- Start ComfyUI with  comfyui h3  (the --fast-disk mode): the text encoder then runs on the GPU in ~30 s instead of ~5 min on the CPU.\n- Any picture size works: the size nodes shrink it to the megapixels you set. 1.0 is fast; 1.5 is sharper but slower.\n- Seed is random each Run. Press Run again for a different take.\n- Clear, front-lit photos where the face is big enough give the best results."
   ],
   "title": "How to use",
   "color": "#b06634",
   "bgcolor": "#353535",
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "HEAD SWAP (BFS LoRA)\n\n1. Picture 1: the body. Its body, pose, outfit, hands, location and lighting stay.\n2. Picture 2: the head. Its face, facial expression, hairstyle and hair color are moved onto the body.\n3. Press Run.\n\nKeep the words 'head_swap:' at the start of the prompt; the BFS LoRA was trained on that wording. Uses the 'alternative' BFS LoRA: in tests the regular v1.1 one left a crosshatch texture over the whole picture. Keep both LoRAs at 1.0; lower strengths gave a broken, noisy image.\n\nTips\n- Start ComfyUI with  comfyui h3  (the --fast-disk mode): the text encoder then runs on the GPU in ~30 s instead of ~5 min on the CPU.\n- Any picture size works: the size nodes shrink it to the megapixels you set. 1.0 is fast; 1.5 is sharper but slower.\n- Seed is random each Run. Press Run again for a different take.\n- Clear, front-lit photos where the face is big enough give the best results."
   }
  },
